{
  "format": "demos-tx-signing-vectors",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Shared transaction-signing vectors, format v1. Copy this file unchanged into the SDK and wallet CIs and check every vector against their own preimage builder and verifier.\nA Demos transaction signature covers the UTF-8 bytes of a preimage. Legacy preimage (signatureDomain inactive): the 64-char lowercase hex tx hash itself. Domain preimage (signatureDomain active): the string demos-tx:v1:<chainId>:<hash> where chainId is the decimal properties.id of the network's genesis. The hash is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of contentJson.\ncontentJson depends on the vector's serialization. 'json': contentJson is JSON.stringify(content) with no whitespace, the serialization where osDenomination is not active (amounts are plain numbers). 'os-string': osDenomination is active; content is what the signer holds (amounts and fees as DEM numbers) and contentJson is the canonical wire form: top-level amount, every transaction_fee field (network_fee, rpc_fee, additional_fee) and every gcr_edits[] amount (balance edits, escrow data.amount, validatorStake amount) become decimal OS strings (DEM x 10^9, no leading zeros), all other fields and the key order stay as they are, then JSON.stringify with no whitespace. Fee keys the signer added beyond the standard ones are kept as written. The two os-string vectors pin the serializer SDK and wallet signers must reproduce; the preimage rules are the same for both serializations.\nTop-level fields: signer.algorithm; signer.publicKeyHex (0x-prefixed ed25519 public key; the key controls nothing and exists only for these vectors); signer.seedLabel (an implementation that wants to regenerate the file derives the 128-byte master seed as SHA-512(seedLabel + ':a') followed by SHA-512(seedLabel + ':b') and passes it to unifiedCrypto.generateIdentity('ed25519', seed); checking the published signatures needs only signer.publicKeyHex).\nPer vector: id, description; serialization ('json' or 'os-string', see above); content (the transaction content object as the signer holds it); contentJson (exact string that was hashed); contentJsonUtf8Hex (the bytes that were hashed, so a non-ASCII vector is unambiguous); hash; signedWith.forkActive and signedWith.chainId (what the signer committed to; chainId is null for the legacy preimage); preimageUtf8 and preimageHex (the exact bytes that were signed); signatureHex (0x-prefixed ed25519 signature over those bytes); hashPresented (the hash the verifier is given, normally equal to hash); verify[] (verifier contexts).\nEach verify entry is { forkActive, chainId, expectedValid }: a verifier whose signatureDomain is (in)active at the transaction's block height and whose genesis properties.id is chainId (null when forkActive is false) must return expectedValid for this signature, using hashPresented as the hash. A conforming implementation builds the preimage from the context, verifies the signature against signer.publicKeyHex and compares with expectedValid. Vectors with expectedValid false are negative vectors and are as binding as the positive ones.",
  "signer": {
    "algorithm": "ed25519",
    "publicKeyHex": "0xf433153c211f4d055a865ca2d8b9015e0eccf4f42cb372d32d68aa3411e07e3d",
    "seedLabel": "demos-tx-signing-vectors-v1 test key, controls nothing"
  },
